---
// An envelope on a wire for the Contact face of the hero cube — the fourth
// and last of the face drawings, same vocabulary as InitialsKWG on Intro,
// BangkokSkyline on Where and DeployPipeline on Craft: strokes only, hairline
// weight, one dot on a path.
//
// It draws the clause the copy opens on. "One door: email" — the route runs
// the full width and the envelope is the one thing standing on it, which is
// the whole claim: a single way in, no forms and no funnel beside it.
//
// The 300 x 128 viewBox is a measurement, not a taste. Contact carries the
// least copy of the four faces — a two-line lede, one mono address, one pill —
// and leaves a 149px band on a 360px face, against Craft's 85 and Where's 101.
// That is the skyline's proportion, not the 52-unit strip Intro and Craft
// share, so this borrows the skyline's frame rather than the pipeline's.
//
// The envelope is centred on y=64 so the route enters and leaves at its
// middle. 120 x 76 leaves air either side; the route is what fills it.
//
// `#route` is load-bearing beyond the drawing: the cube script in index.astro
// runs the dot along it as a motion path. It spans the full frame, so the loop
// seam falls off the edge where nobody sees it.
---

<svg
  class="envelope"
  viewBox="0 0 300 128"
  fill="none"
  preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet"
  aria-hidden="true"
  focusable="false"
  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
>
  <!-- The route stops at the envelope rather than running through it. A mask
       does that with nothing painted, which an opaque fill could not: every
       face is transparent now, and a filled box is the one thing on a
       see-through wall that still reads as a panel. It also leaves #route one
       unbroken path, so it stays usable as a motion path and DrawSVG keeps
       ownership of its stroke-dasharray. maskUnits is explicit because the
       default region is a share of the object's bounding box, and a
       horizontal line's box is zero-height. -->
  <defs>
    <mask id="route-gap" maskUnits="userSpaceOnUse" x="0" y="0" width="300" height="128">
      <rect x="0" y="0" width="300" height="128" fill="#fff" />
      <rect x="90" y="26" width="120" height="76" fill="#000" />
    </mask>
  </defs>

  <!-- The route first, so the envelope sits over it rather than under. -->
  <path
    id="route"
    class="envelope__line envelope__route"
    data-draw
    mask="url(#route-gap)"
    d="M0 64 H300"
  />

  <!-- The envelope: the body, then the flap folded down into it. -->
  <path class="envelope__line" data-draw d="M90 26 H210 V102 H90 Z" />
  <path class="envelope__line" data-draw d="M90 26 L150 68 L210 26" />

  <!-- Parked at the origin and hidden until the script places it on the route:
       with no JS there is no stray dot in the corner. -->
  <circle class="envelope__dot" data-mover="route" cx="0" cy="0" r="1.8" />
</svg>

<style lang="scss">
  // Fills the positioned box the face gives it and scales to fit. Absolute
  // rather than a percentage height, which does not resolve against a flex
  // item's box.
  .envelope {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    display: block;
    // Both explicitly, not left to `inset`: an SVG is a replaced element, so
    // an auto height resolves to its intrinsic one and the bottom offset is
    // dropped. Sized this way the viewBox letterboxes to fit instead.
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    color: var(--c-hairline-bright);
  }

  .envelope__line {
    fill: none;
    stroke: currentColor;
    stroke-width: 1;
    // The face scales with the viewport; the stroke must not. A hairline is a
    // hairline at every size or it stops being one.
    vector-effect: non-scaling-stroke;
  }

  // The route sits back from the envelope so the envelope stays the subject —
  // the same relation the river has to the skyline and the wire to its nodes.
  .envelope__route {
    opacity: 0.55;
  }

  .envelope__dot {
    fill: #fff;
    visibility: hidden;
  }
</style>
